  "worked_solution": "As the higher-order partial derivatives are continuous on an open set $U,$ the mixed partial derivatives must be equal. Hence, we have\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{f}_{yxy}(x,y) & ={f}_{xyy}(x,y) \\\\  & =\\frac{\u2202}{\u2202y}({f}_{xy}(x,y)) \\\\  & =\\frac{\u2202}{\u2202y}(7+x\\operatorname{sin}\u2061y) \\\\  & =x\\operatorname{cos}\u2061y.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nNow, we evaluate the partial derivative at the point $(6,\\frac{\\pi }{3}):$\n\n$$\n{f}_{yxy}(6,\\frac{\\pi }{3})=6\\cdot \\operatorname{cos}\u2061(\\frac{\\pi }{3})=3\n$$",
